course: dictionary
lesson: 1947
title: Commonly and what it tells us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Commonly means usually, or often, or in many places. When you see it, the writer is telling you something happens a lot, but not always. «The collarbone is one of the most commonly broken bones in children» means many children break it, more than many other bones, but not every child does.
explain: Look at the words near it for clues. «Most commonly» points to the top one in a group. «Commonly known as» means usually called by this name, as in «Tyrannosaurus rex, commonly known as T. rex.»
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in usually or often. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it. «It usually heals well in a few weeks» tells you the collarbone is often mended quickly, which is good news.
fact: Commonly means usually or often, by many people or in many places.
fact: «Commonly known as» means usually called by this name.
fact: «Most commonly» means the one that happens most often.
fact: In maths, the most commonly chosen colour is the mode: the answer that appears most often.
fact: In science, plants and animals are often commonly called by everyday names instead of Latin ones.
exercise: «Tyrannosaurus rex, commonly known as T. rex, was a huge dinosaur.» What does commonly known as mean? | Written in Latin only | Never heard of by anyone | Found only in one small town | *Usually called by this name
exercise: Plants and animals are commonly called by everyday names. What does commonly mean here? | Never | Only once | Quietly | *Usually
exercise: «The collarbone is one of the most commonly broken bones in children.» What does most commonly mean? | Happening in a hospital | Happening only in winter | *Happening most often | Happening least often
test: Which word in «Dandelions are commonly found on lawns» means often? | lawns | found | *commonly | dandelions
test: In a class vote, the most commonly chosen colour was blue. What does this tell us? | Blue was picked by one child only | *Blue was picked more often than any other colour | Blue was not picked at all
exam: Which sentence uses commonly to mean usually? | The commonly book is green | Commonly she is a dog | *Colds are commonly caught in winter | Commonly the sun shines at night
